claim.claim-text:
inserting the bougie (10) into a stomach (B) of a patient until the guiding segment (120) is positioned along a lesser curve of the stomach (B);
displacing the sheath (60) with respect to the bougie (10) in a backward direction to expose the guiding segment (120);
joining opposed walls of the stomach (B) along a junction line in response to a position of the guiding segment (120) in the stomach to form the sleeve (G) within the stomach (B);
displacing the sheath (60) with respect to the bougie (10) in a forward direction to cover the guiding segment (120); and
removing the bougie (10) from the stomach (B).
